{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/dijkstrasearchevent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SQ","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SH","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DijkstraSearchEvent"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Weight"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each source is discovered first, at distance zero. Then, while a discovered vertex is not yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"settled, the one with the smallest distance is examined (settled at that distance), and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its out-edges is examined in turn with the distance it offers its target: the examined"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s distance plus the edge’s weight. An edge into an unsettled target is then relaxed,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the offer is smaller than the target’s distance or the target was not yet discovered, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not relaxed. A relaxed edge to an undiscovered target is followed by that target’s discovery."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"An edge into a settled vertex, a self-loop included, is examined and nothing more. After its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"last out-edge the examined vertex is finished. Vertices the sources do not reach are never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearch.swift#L17","fileName":"DijkstraSearch.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths19DijkstraSearchEventO","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DijkstraSearchEvent"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"DijkstraSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"enum","title":"DijkstraSearchEvent"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a Dijkstra search reports, in order, with the events of the Boost Graph Library’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Dijkstra visitor."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent\/discover(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent\/edgeNotRelaxed(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/docu